{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <queue>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n#include <utility>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007;\nconst int INF = 0x3f3f3f3f;\n\nstruct Edge {\n    int dest, cap, cost, revIdx;\n    Edge(int d, int c, int cs, int r) : dest(d), cap(c), cost(cs), revIdx(r) {}\n};\n\nstruct MCMF {\n    int N;\n    vector<vector<Edge>> gph;\n    vector<int> dist, prevV, prevE;\n    \n    MCMF(int n) : N(n), gph(n) {\n        dist.resize(n);\n        prevV.resize(n);\n        prevE.resize(n);\n    }\n    \n    void addEdge(int from, int to, int capacity, int cost) {\n        gph[from].emplace_back(to, capacity, cost, (int)gph[to].size());\n        gph[to].emplace_back(from, 0, -cost, (int)gph[from].size()-1);\n    }\n    \n    bool shortestPath(int src, int dst) {\n        fill(dist.begin(), dist.end(), INF);\n        dist[src] = 0;\n        vector<bool> inq(N, false);\n        queue<int> q;\n        q.push(src);\n        inq[src] = true;\n        \n        while (!q.empty()) {\n            int u = q.front(); q.pop();\n            inq[u] = false;\n            \n            for (int i = 0; i < gph[u].size(); ++i) {\n                auto &e = gph[u][i];\n                if (e.cap > 0 && dist[e.dest] > dist[u] + e.cost) {\n                    dist[e.dest] = dist[u] + e.cost;\n                    prevV[e.dest] = u;\n                    prevE[e.dest] = i;\n                    if (!inq[e.dest]) {\n                        inq[e.dest] = true;\n                        q.push(e.dest);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return dist[dst] < INF;\n    }\n    \n    int compute(int s, int t) {\n        int totalCost = 0;\n        while (shortestPath(s, t)) {\n            int flow = INF;\n            for (int v = t; v != s; v = prevV[v]) {\n                flow = min(flow, gph[prevV[v]][prevE[v]].cap);\n            }\n            totalCost += dist[t] * flow;\n            for (int v = t; v != s; v = prevV[v]) {\n                auto &e = gph[prevV[v]][prevE[v]];\n                e.cap -= flow;\n                gph[v][e.revIdx].cap += flow;\n            }\n        }\n        return totalCost;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    int n, m, k, c, d;\n    cin >> n >> m >> k >> c >> d;\n    \n    int src = 0;\n    int dst = n * 100 + 1;\n    MCMF mcmf(dst + 1);\n    \n    // Connect all nodes at level 100 to sink\n    for (int level = 1; level <= 100; ++level) {\n        mcmf.addEdge(level, dst, 100, 0);\n    }\n    \n    // Connect source to starting positions\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n        int startPos;\n        cin >> startPos;\n        mcmf.addEdge(src, (startPos - 1) * 100 + 1, 1, 0);\n    }\n    \n    // Connect positions within same node: i -> i+1\n    for (int node = 1; node <= n; ++node) {\n        for (int level = 1; level < 100; ++level) {\n            int from = (node - 1) * 100 + level;\n            int to = (node - 1) * 100 + level + 1;\n            mcmf.addEdge(from, to, 100, c);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Connect positions between nodes\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\n        int u, v;\n        cin >> u >> v;\n        \n        for (int level = 1; level < 100; ++level) {\n            int fromU = (u - 1) * 100 + level;\n            int toV = (v - 1) * 100 + level + 1;\n            for (int step = 1; step <= 50; ++step) {\n                int edgeCost = c + (step * step - (step - 1) * (step - 1)) * d;\n                mcmf.addEdge(fromU, toV, 1, edgeCost);\n            }\n        }\n        \n        for (int level = 1; level < 100; ++level) {\n            int fromV = (v - 1) * 100 + level;\n            int toU = (u - 1) * 100 + level + 1;\n            for (int step = 1; step <= 50; ++step) {\n                int edgeCost = c + (step * step - (step - 1) * (step - 1)) * d;\n                mcmf.addEdge(fromV, toU, 1, edgeCost);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << mcmf.compute(src, dst) << '\\n';\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\nINF = 0x3f3f3f3f\n\nclass Edge:\n    def __init__(self, dest, cap, cost, revIdx):\n        self.dest = dest\n        self.cap = cap\n        self.cost = cost\n        self.revIdx = revIdx\n\nclass MCMF:\n    def __init__(self, n):\n        self.N = n\n        self.gph = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n        self.dist = [INF] * n\n        self.prevV = [0] * n\n        self.prevE = [0] * n\n    \n    def addEdge(self, from_node, to_node, capacity, cost):\n        revIdx_to = len(self.gph[to_node])\n        revIdx_from = len(self.gph[from_node])\n        self.gph[from_node].append(Edge(to_node, capacity, cost, revIdx_to))\n        self.gph[to_node].append(Edge(from_node, 0, -cost, revIdx_from))\n    \n    def shortestPath(self, src, dst):\n        self.dist = [INF] * self.N\n        self.dist[src] = 0\n        inq = [False] * self.N\n        q = deque()\n        q.append(src)\n        inq[src] = True\n        \n        while q:\n            u = q.popleft()\n            inq[u] = False\n            \n            for i in range(len(self.gph[u])):\n                e = self.gph[u][i]\n                if e.cap > 0 and self.dist[e.dest] > self.dist[u] + e.cost:\n                    self.dist[e.dest] = self.dist[u] + e.cost\n                    self.prevV[e.dest] = u\n                    self.prevE[e.dest] = i\n                    if not inq[e.dest]:\n                        inq[e.dest] = True\n                        q.append(e.dest)\n        return self.dist[dst] < INF\n    \n    def compute(self, s, t):\n        totalCost = 0\n        while self.shortestPath(s, t):\n            flow = INF\n            v = t\n            while v != s:\n                u = self.prevV[v]\n                idx = self.prevE[v]\n                flow = min(flow, self.gph[u][idx].cap)\n                v = u\n            \n            totalCost += self.dist[t] * flow\n            \n            v = t\n            while v != s:\n                u = self.prevV[v]\n                idx = self.prevE[v]\n                e = self.gph[u][idx]\n                e.cap -= flow\n                rev_e = self.gph[v][e.revIdx]\n                rev_e.cap += flow\n                v = u\n        \n        return totalCost\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    k = int(data[2])\n    c = int(data[3])\n    d = int(data[4])\n    \n    src = 0\n    dst = n * 100 + 1\n    mcmf = MCMF(dst + 1)\n    \n    # Connect all nodes at level 100 to sink\n    for level in range(1, 101):\n        mcmf.addEdge(level, dst, 100, 0)\n    \n    # Connect source to starting positions\n    idx = 5\n    for _ in range(k):\n        startPos = int(data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n        mcmf.addEdge(src, (startPos - 1) * 100 + 1, 1, 0)\n    \n    # Connect positions within same node: i -> i+1\n    for node in range(1, n + 1):\n        for level in range(1, 100):\n            from_node = (node - 1) * 100 + level\n            to_node = (node - 1) * 100 + level + 1\n            mcmf.addEdge(from_node, to_node, 100, c)\n    \n    # Connect positions between nodes\n    for _ in range(m):\n        u = int(data[idx])\n        v = int(data[idx + 1])\n        idx += 2\n        \n        for level in range(1, 100):\n            fromU = (u - 1) * 100 + level\n            toV = (v - 1) * 100 + level + 1\n            for step in range(1, 51):\n                edgeCost = c + (step * step - (step - 1) * (step - 1)) * d\n                mcmf.addEdge(fromU, toV, 1, edgeCost)\n        \n        for level in range(1, 100):\n            fromV = (v - 1) * 100 + level\n            toU = (u - 1) * 100 + level + 1\n            for step in range(1, 51):\n                edgeCost = c + (step * step - (step - 1) * (step - 1)) * d\n                mcmf.addEdge(fromV, toU, 1, edgeCost)\n    \n    print(mcmf.compute(src, dst))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013028726971242577, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.1151231974363327, -0.0032772899139672518, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.0005547653418034315, -0.000301673193462193, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.0007175016799010336, -0.00642744917422533, -0.6869012713432312, -0.00015436411194968969, -0.0059540290385484695, -0.0031780709978193045, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -1.1086402082582936e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.05564855504781e-05, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.5237331986427307, -0.0005943200667388737, -2.098061486321967e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.5759400725364685, -8.344646857949556e-07, -5.722029527532868e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -4.8040190449682996e-